&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THRIVE MARKET&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Thrive Market was founded in 2014 with a mission to make healthy and sustainable living easy and affordable for everyone. As an online, membership-based market, we deliver the highest quality healthy, and sustainable products at member-only prices, while matching every paid membership with a free one for someone in need. Every day, we leverage innovative technology and member-first thinking to help our over 1,600,000+ members find better products, support better brands, and build a better world in the process. We are also a Certified B Corporation, a Public Benefit Corporation, and a Climate Neutral Certified company.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Join us as we bring healthy and sustainable living to millions of Americans in the years to come.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;As an &lt;strong&gt;Area Manager&lt;/strong&gt;, you will lead and manage multiple teams responsible for achieving operational goals and fostering strong stakeholder relationships. You’ll oversee the effectiveness of Fulfillment Center strategies and ensure the quality of your team’s deliverables. This role is pivotal in driving team success, promoting a culture of inclusion, and aligning your team’s efforts with broader organizational objectives. You&#39;ll leverage your knowledge and leadership to optimize operations, manage risks, and support your team’s growth and development.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCHEDULE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;To Be Determined (&lt;em&gt;overtime as needed to support the business, and must be willing to cover other shifts when needed&lt;/em&gt;)&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot; data-qa=&quot;preview-list-item-0&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 data-qa=&quot;preview-list-item-0-text&quot;&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have managerial oversight of a team responsible for achieving operational goals and fostering strong stakeholder relationships. Ensure the effective implementation of Fulfillment Center strategies and maintain the highest quality standards in team deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a positive and inclusive work environment aligned with Thrive Market&#39;s core values. Recognize and celebrate team achievements, promoting a culture of excellence and belonging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize operational excellence by optimizing team metrics, processes, and best practices. Ensure compliance with policies and allocate resources effectively to set up operational metrics. Identify and address root causes, automate where possible, and focus on projects that enhance deliverable quality and team environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and develop your team to encourage skill growth, independent decision-making, and active participation in discussions. Assign tasks strategically to stretch and develop team members, and review work to ensure consistency, accuracy, and alignment with goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify and mitigate risks, resolve blockers, and manage team commitments. Prevent over-commitment and effectively scope efforts to address challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain open and transparent communication with partner teams, stakeholders, and management. Share priorities, status updates, and team challenges, ensuring everyone understands decision-making processes and changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audit performance to ensure effective results and make data-driven decisions. Document lessons learned to prevent recurring issues and contribute to continuous improvement in operational practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain a deep understanding of the products your team works with and foster collaborative relationships with partner teams. Provide guidance on operational excellence and support your team in achieving high performance standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be willing to work in a cold / freezer work environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be comfortable working in a multi-temperature environment ranging from -10 degrees to 40 degrees Fahrenheit and outside ambient temperatures (including heat and cold)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot; data-qa=&quot;preview-list-item-1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 data-qa=&quot;preview-list-item-1-text&quot;&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s Degree or 5+ years of leadership experience in Fulfillment, Distribution, or Warehouse operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced functional knowledge of supply chain management, including fulfillment, procurement, transportation, and warehousing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in managing teams, influencing stakeholders, and driving strategic initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, problem-solving, and decision-making skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication abilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage complex problems, mitigate risks, and make strategic trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in coaching, developing team members, and fostering a culture of inclusion and collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot; data-qa=&quot;preview-list-item-2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 data-qa=&quot;preview-list-item-2-text&quot;&gt;BELONG TO A BETTER COMPANY&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive health benefits (medical, dental, vision, life, and disability)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive pay + equity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunities for advancement. We have programs that will start you on a path and train you along the way&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coverage for Life Coaching &amp;amp; Therapy Sessions on our holistic mental health and well-being platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free Thrive Market membership and discount on private label products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Casual atmosphere and great people to work with&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We&#39;re a community of more than 1 Million + members who are united by a singular belief: It should be easy to find better&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;products, support better brands, make better choices, and build a better world in the process.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;At Thrive Market, we believe in building a diverse, inclusive, and authentic culture. If you are excited about this role along with our mission and values, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;Thrive Market is an EEO/Veterans/Disabled/LGBTQ employer&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Thrive Market, our goal is to be a diverse and inclusive workplace that is representative, at all job levels, of the members we serve and the communities we operate in. We’re proud to be an inclusive company and an Equal Opportunity Employer and we prohibit discrimination and harassment of any kind. We believe that diversity and inclusion among our teammates is critical to our success as a company, and we seek to recruit, develop and retain the most talented people from a diverse candidate pool. If you’re thinking about joining our team, we expect that you would agree!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you need assistance or accommodation due to a disability, please email us at eeo@thrivemarket.com and we’ll be happy to assist you.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Ensure your Thrive Market job offer is legitimate and don&#39;t fall victim to fraud. Thrive Market never seeks payment from job&amp;nbsp;applicants. Thrive Market recruiters will only reach out to applicants from an @thrivemarket.com email address. For added&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;security, where possible, apply through our company website at.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;© Thrive Market 2026 All rights reserved.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot; data-qa=&quot;preview-list-item-3&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 data-qa=&quot;preview-list-item-3-text&quot;&gt;JOB INFORMATION&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compensation Description - The starting salary range for this position is between $50K-$65K.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salary may increase over time based upon: skill, level of responsibility, additional duties, seniority, quantity or quality of production, or other legitimate, business-related factors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Total Compensation includes Base Salary, Stock Options, Health and Wellness Benefits, and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THRIVE MARKET&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thrive Market was founded in 2014 with a mission to make healthy and sustainable living easy and affordable for everyone. As an online, membership-based market, we deliver the highest quality healthy, and sustainable products at member-only prices, while matching every paid membership with a free one for someone in need. Every day, we leverage innovative technology and member-first thinking to help our over 1,700,000+ members find better products, support better brands, and build a better world in the process. We are also a Certified B Corporation, a Public Benefit Corporation, and a Climate Neutral Certified company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us as we bring healthy and sustainable living to millions of Americans in the years to come.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Art Director of Packaging leads the creative strategy, quality, and consistency of Thrive Market’s Owned Brands packaging. This role manages a team of designers and production artists, collaborates cross-functionally to align packaging with brand goals, and oversees the production process from concept to print. Additionally, the Art Director drives innovation, optimizes design workflows, and ensures packaging meets industry trends and consumer expectations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is organized, process-oriented, has extreme attention to detail, and thrives in a fast-paced working environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Creative Vision and Art Direction:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive quality and consistency across all Thrive Market Owned Brands, providing daily creative feedback to the design team and aligning with stakeholders in bi-weekly meetings. Ensure all packaging designs adhere to brand standards and contribute to a cohesive brand identity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Management and Development: &lt;/strong&gt;Oversee a team of packaging designers, delegating projects effectively and setting team members up for success. Conduct mid-year and annual performance reviews, manage career pathing, and establish clear OKRs (Objectives and Key Results) to support growth and skill development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mentorship and Skill Building: &lt;/strong&gt;Mentor designers, helping them optimize their processes, develop creative efficiencies, and achieve high standards in their work. Inspire team members through constructive feedback and fostering a collaborative team environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration: &lt;/strong&gt;Partner with teams in photo, content, and merchandising marketing to define creative objectives, packaging style, and strategic approaches. Interpret and follow Creative Briefs closely to ensure packaging aligns with broader brand and product objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Editorial and Content Alignment: &lt;/strong&gt;Collaborate with the Content team to define the editorial direction for packaging, ensuring that brand storytelling aligns seamlessly across all packaging touchpoints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brand Style Guides:&lt;/strong&gt; Build, manage, and update brand style guides, including packaging standards (such as substrates, design elements, and typography) to maintain a strong visual identity across all Thrive Market brands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Production Oversight: &lt;/strong&gt;Manage the production process from design to printing, identifying and flagging any design inconsistencies and ensuring quality through all production stages. Collaborate with production teams on mechanicals and printing best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proofing and Press Checks: &lt;/strong&gt;Review proofs and lead press checks (on-site or remote), approving or rejecting against brand standards and printer specifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;New Product Development: &lt;/strong&gt;Provide creative support for product development, particularly for new categories like home goods, textiles, and specialty products, ensuring alignment with the overall brand aesthetic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market and Competitive Research:&lt;/strong&gt; Conduct ongoing competitive research to stay informed about industry trends and consumer preferences, bringing innovative ideas to enhance Thrive Market&#39;s presence in the packaging space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Optimization:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and implement operational efficiencies to streamline the packaging design process, reducing unnecessary revisions and improving productivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Presentation and Leadership Communication: &lt;/strong&gt;Create presentation materials, including packaging mockups and competitive landscape analysis, for leadership review, ensuring clear communication of strategic decisions and design rationale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Photography and Retouching Oversight: &lt;/strong&gt;Guide the on-pack photography process, providing direction and retouching feedback to ensure consistency and quality across all product images.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation in Packaging: &lt;/strong&gt;Identify new opportunities to elevate the Thrive Market brand within the packaging industry by staying current on best practices in design, printing, and branding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 5+ years in packaging design and art direction, with a strong background in brand development, preferably within the CPG, food, or wellness industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership Skills: &lt;/strong&gt;Proven experience managing a creative team, including mentorship, performance reviews, and project delegation, with a minimum of 2 years of direct people management experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Proficiency in Adobe Creative Suite (Illustrator, Photoshop, InDesign) and knowledge of print production processes, packaging substrates, and materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design Systems:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven experience building, documenting, and maintaining scalable packaging design systems (templates, modular layouts, typography, color, substrates, and component libraries) that keep multiple product lines and brands cohesive and speed up production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proofing &amp;amp; Press Checks: &lt;/strong&gt;Hands-on experience with proofing workflows and on-site or remote press checks, including color-matching, evaluating print quality, and approving or rejecting proofs against brand standards and printer specs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Tools &amp;amp; Efficiency: &lt;/strong&gt;Experience evaluating and implementing AI tools to increase team efficiency, including assessing fit, quality, and risk, and integrating approved tools into design and production workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Photography &amp;amp; Retouching:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience directing on-pack product photography and giving retouching feedback to maintain consistent image quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Creative Vision:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong eye for design, typography, and color; ability to create cohesive brand identities and maintain quality standards across multiple products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration: &lt;/strong&gt;Demonstrated ability to work with cross-functional teams, including content, photography, product development, and merchandising, to align packaging with overall brand and product goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project Management: &lt;/strong&gt;Excellent organizational skills to manage multiple projects, timelines, and deadlines in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market Knowledge:&lt;/strong&gt; Understanding of current trends in packaging, sustainability, and consumer behavior, with the ability to conduct competitive research and apply insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong verbal and written communication abilities for presenting design concepts and rationale to stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem-Solving:&lt;/strong&gt; Skilled in identifying and addressing design inconsistencies and production issues, with a proactive approach to improving design processes and workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education: &lt;/strong&gt;A bachelor’s degree in Graphic Design, Visual Arts, or a related field is preferred, though equivalent professional experience may also be considered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BELONG TO A BETTER COMPANY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive health benefits (medical, dental, vision, life and disability)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary (DOE) + equity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401k plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;9 Observed Holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized ClassPass Membership with access to fitness classes and wellness and beauty experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in our beautiful office in Playa Vista&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free Thrive Market membership with exclusive employee discount&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coverage for Life Coaching &amp;amp; Therapy Sessions on our holistic mental health and well-being platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a community of more than 1 Million + members who are united by a singular belief: It should be easy to find better products, support better brands, make better choices, and build a better world in the process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Thrive Market, we believe in building a diverse, inclusive, and authentic culture. If you are excited about this role along with our mission and values, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Thrive Market is an EEO/Veterans/Disabled/LGBTQ employer&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Thrive Market, our goal is to be a diverse and inclusive workplace that is representative, at all job levels, of the members we serve and the communities we operate in. We’re proud to be an inclusive company and an Equal Opportunity Employer and we prohibit discrimination and harassment of any kind. We believe that diversity and inclusion among our teammates is critical to our success as a company, and we seek to recruit, develop and retain the most talented people from a diverse candidate pool. If you’re thinking about joining our team, we expect that you would agree!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Employment with Thrive Market requires that employees be based in the United States. This is a condition of employment and must be maintained throughout the duration of employment.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you need assistance or accommodation due to a disability, please email us at eeo@thrivemarket.com and we’ll be happy to assist you.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ensure your Thrive Market job offer is legitimate and don&#39;t fall victim to fraud. Thrive Market never seeks payment from job applicants. Thrive Market recruiters will only reach out to applicants from an @thrivemarket.com email address. For added security, where possible, apply through our company website at &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.thrivemarket.com/&quot;&gt;www.thrivemarket.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;© Thrive Market 2026 All rights reserved.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;JOB INFORMATION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compensation Description - The base salary range for this position is $100,000 - $125,000/Per Year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compensation may vary outside of this range depending on several factors, including a candidate’s qualifications, skills, competencies and experience, and geographic location.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Total Compensation includes Base Salary, Stock Options, Health &amp;amp; Wellness Benefits, Flexible PTO, and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position requires traveling to our HQ office in Los Angeles, California, twice a year for all-company summits; once in the summer and once in the winter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THRIVE MARKET&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Thrive Market was founded in 2014 with a mission to make healthy and sustainable living easy and affordable for everyone. As an online, membership-based market, we deliver the highest quality healthy, and sustainable products at member-only prices, while matching every paid membership with a free one for someone in need. Every day, we leverage innovative technology and member-first thinking to help our over 1,700,000+ members find better products, support better brands, and build a better world in the process. We are also a Certified B Corporation, a Public Benefit Corporation, and a Climate Neutral Certified company.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Join us as we bring healthy and sustainable living to millions of Americans in the years to come.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; Thrive Market is on a mission to make healthy and sustainable living easy and affordable for everyone. As we enter our next phase of growth, acquisition marketing is a major focus, and paid social plays a critical role in driving new member growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring an Associate Director, Paid Social Acquisition to own and scale our paid social program, with Meta and TikTok as core channels and Pinterest, Snapchat, and emerging platforms as additional growth levers. This person will set cross-platform strategy, allocate budget against incremental returns, build the signal and measurement foundation that powers platform optimization, and lead experimentation that turns insight into sustained member growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a strong fit for someone who combines deep hands-on platform expertise with analytical rigor and sound marketing judgment, enjoys operating with autonomy, and can lead people, partners, and cross-functional teams. This role reports to the Senior Director of Member Growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own paid social acquisition strategy and performance, with Meta and TikTok as core channels, and grow Pinterest, Snapchat, and emerging platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Allocate and reallocate multi-million-dollar budgets across platforms based on marginal and incremental returns, not platform-reported performance alone. Own forecasting, pacing, and planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead signal engineering: Conversions API and server-side tracking, event match quality, deduplication, backend and offline conversion events, value-based and predicted-LTV optimization, and first-party audience strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Analytics and Engineering to build reliable conversion signals, reconcile platform, attribution, and backend data, and improve data quality across platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and run incrementality measurement, including platform conversion lift studies, geo holdouts, and MMM inputs, and use results to guide investment decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set testing priorities and lead experimentation across audiences, creative, formats, bidding strategies, and account structure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and run a structured creative testing program across studio, UGC, creators, and partnership ads, including AI-assisted creative production. Write briefs and influence creative direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and develop one direct report, and hold agency and platform partners accountable for strategy, execution, and results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze performance and creative data to identify drivers, risks, and growth opportunities, and translate insights into clear recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor platform changes, privacy and signal shifts, industry trends, and competitive dynamics, and apply them to strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate performance, learnings, trade-offs, and investment recommendations clearly to senior leadership and cross-functional partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years in performance or growth marketing, with deep expertise in paid social.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level, hands-on experience managing and scaling Meta campaigns, including account structure, Advantage+, bidding, and creative testing at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level, hands-on experience managing and scaling TikTok, including Smart+ and Spark Ads, creator and native creative, and the TikTok Events API.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience with Pinterest and allocating multi-million-dollar budgets across platforms. Snapchat, Reddit, and Google experience a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High proficiency in signal engineering: Conversions API, server-side tracking, event match quality, offline and backend conversion integration, and value-based bidding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and interpreting incrementality tests (conversion lift, geo holdouts) and working with MMM and multi-touch attribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of leading structured creative testing programs and influencing creative direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing and developing direct reports, and managing agency or platform partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills, with the ability to translate complex data into clear, actionable recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in subscription or e-commerce businesses. Health, grocery, or wellness experience is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, influential communicator who can articulate performance drivers, trade-offs, and recommendations to executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating with ambiguity and taking ownership in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent relevant experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-qa=&quot;preview-list-item-2-text&quot;&gt;BELONG TO A BETTER COMPANY&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive health benefits (medical, dental, vision, life and disability)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary (DOE) + equity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401k plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;9 Observed Holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized ClassPass Membership with access to fitness classes and wellness and beauty experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in our beautiful office in Playa Vista&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free Thrive Market membership with exclusive employee discount&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coverage for Life Coaching &amp;amp; Therapy Sessions on our holistic mental health and well-being platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We&#39;re a community of more than 1 Million + members who are united by a singular belief: It should be easy to find better products, support better brands, make better choices, and build a better world in the process.&lt;/div&gt;
