&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thrive Market is looking for a Senior Accountant to join our growing, fully remote Accounting team. This is an excellent opportunity to professionally develop within a fast-paced, mission-driven company. The candidate is responsible for maintaining timely, accurate financial records and performing other day-to-day activities and ad hoc projects on the accounting team. The position will assume ownership of a wide range of account reconciliations, financial closing activities, and other projects to support our financial close process. The candidate for the Senior Accountant position must have an advanced understanding of financial statements (balance sheet, income statement, and cash flow) and how they relate to one another. Candidates must also have a working knowledge of US GAAP and internal controls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is self-motivated, has a keen eye for detail, and works independently and reliably with team members throughout various levels of the company. This role will report to the Accounting Manager.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for monthly financial closing activities, procedures, journal entries, and account reconciliations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support month-end and year-end close activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and review financial activity , as well as assist with flux analysis, to help ensure transactions are recorded timely and accurately&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with internal teams and external business contacts to support accurate and timely financial processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with the annual financial audit and related documentation requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take on ad-hoc accounting projects and other duties as needed to support the Accounting and Finance team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize accounting systems and tools to process, record, and maintain financial transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5 years in FP&amp;amp;A, strategic finance, investment banking, consulting, or a related analytical field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s Degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in e-commerce, retail, or CPG is a plus&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Excel skills and comfort with complex financial modeling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills with the ability to manipulate and interpret large data sets to draw actionable insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SQL or BI tools (Domo, Tableau, etc.) strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ERP/planning/forecasting/reporting tools (NetSuite, Adaptive, etc.) strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills and the ability to collaborate cross-functionally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized with a strong attention to detail and an ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
