&lt;li&gt;MBA with a focus in analytics, strategy, or a related quantitative field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate business questions into analytical frameworks and provide actionable, prescriptive insights to stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in SQL and data visualization tools (e.g., Domo, Looker, Tableau) with a focus on self-serve dashboard governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced SQL skills with experience in cloud data warehouses (Snowflake, BigQuery).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using DBT and Python for data manipulation, transformation, and processing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong foundation in statistics and multivariate regression.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in building and interpreting member segmentation models to drive personalized lifecycle campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of designing, executing, and analyzing complex A/B and multivariate tests across channels (email, SMS, push, onsite).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to connect CRM metrics (e.g., retention, LTV, churn, reactivation, ROAS) to overall business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to clearly communicate insights to non-technical audiences and influence decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating with CRM, product, and data engineering teams to influence experimentation design, campaign strategy, and measurement frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of data quality, attribution, and causal inference techniques in the context of CRM performance measurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious, collaborative, and highly self-motivated — with a bias for action and a business-first mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in eCommerce or subscription businesses is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
